# Installation Walkthrough

## Changes Made

### VS Code
- Downloaded the official User Installer from Microsoft.
- Performed a silent installation to `C:\dev\Microsoft VS Code`.
- Verified installation with `code --version`.

### Coolify
- Executed the Coolify v4 installation script within the `Ubuntu` WSL distribution.
- Verified that all necessary containers (sentinel, coolify, etc.) are running and healthy.
- Confirmed that the Coolify dashboard is accessible on `localhost:8000`.

## Verification Results

### VS Code
```powershell
code --version
1.112.0
07ff9d6178ede9a1bd12ad3399074d726ebe6e43
x64
```

### Coolify
The dashboard is active and responding:
```powershell
StatusCode        : 200
StatusDescription : OK
```
You can access it at [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000).

> [!NOTE]
> Coolify instances running local to your machine will use Docker Desktop's engine. Ensure Docker Desktop is always running when using Coolify.
